            <div xml:id="d177">

                <pb facs="0323" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg263"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Webb to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 58.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Petropolis,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-02-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 6, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: General Asboth, the United States minister
                    resident at Buenos Ayres, died on the 21st January.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I sent to the Presidents of the Argentine and Uruguayan Republics copies of my
                    communication to the government of Brazil, renewing the <pb facs="0324" n="264"
                        xml:id="pg264"/> tender of good offices. You will find a copy of my letter
                    inclosed, marked B.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. WATSON WEBB.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d177-a1.xml" xpointer="d177-a1"/>
